What I Did (Methods)
I set up my Census API key locally and loaded the needed packages (tidycensus, tigris, sf, dplyr, ggplot2, tidyr, stringr, knitr, scales). I focused on Washington State at the county level and selected:

Median gross rent (B25064_001), and
Households with SNAP benefits (B22010_002).

I downloaded ACS 2019–2023 (5-year) data with geometry, reshaped to a wide table (estimates + MOEs), then made a map for rent and tables for SNAP counts.


Code
vars &lt;- c(
  rent = "B25064_001",
  snap = "B22010_002"
)

wa_raw &lt;- get_acs(
  geography = "county",
  state = "WA",
  variables = vars,
  year = 2023,
  survey = "acs5",
  geometry = TRUE
)

geom_tbl &lt;- wa_raw |&gt;
  dplyr::select(GEOID, geometry) |&gt;
  sf::st_as_sf() |&gt;
  dplyr::distinct(GEOID, .keep_all = TRUE)

acs_wide &lt;- wa_raw |&gt;
  sf::st_drop_geometry() |&gt;
  dplyr::select(GEOID, NAME, variable, estimate, moe) |&gt;
  tidyr::pivot_wider(
    names_from = variable,
    values_from = c(estimate, moe),
    names_glue = "{.value}_{variable}"
  ) |&gt;
  dplyr::rename(
    estimate_rent_median = estimate_rent,
    moe_rent_median      = moe_rent,
    estimate_snap_hh     = estimate_snap,
    moe_snap_hh          = moe_snap
  ) |&gt;
  dplyr::mutate(
    county = stringr::str_replace(NAME, ", Washington", "")
  ) |&gt;
  dplyr::left_join(geom_tbl, by = "GEOID") |&gt;
  sf::st_as_sf()
